  "id": "COMPOUND:24902 - PROTEIN:5837",
  "verbalization": "Phyllofolactones F appears to act as a common target for multiple compounds that ultimately lead to the inhibition of SN12K1. These compounds, including Opposit-4(15)-Ene-1Beta,11-Diol, 2-(1a,4-dimethyl-3,3a,4,5,6,7,7a,7b-octahydro-2H-naphtho[1,2-b]oxiren-7-yl)prop-2-enoic acid, and Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, all share a common target of T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3. This suggests that Phyllofolactones F may modulate CD3 through a shared mechanism, potentially affecting downstream signaling pathways. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Phyllofolactones F and SN12K1, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways converging on SN12K1 indicates a potential role in cellular processes involving T-cell activation or signaling, which could be relevant in therapeutic contexts.",
